menu "Michi Music Stream Button"

    comment "Deterministic gestures (contract in michi_button_gesture.h): short press (< RECOVERY_PRESS_MS) opens the pairing window; long press (>= RECOVERY_PRESS_MS and < FACTORY_RESET_PRESS_MS) runs recovery ONLY in RECOVERABLE_ERROR; very long press (>= FACTORY_RESET_PRESS_MS) runs the factory reset (armed). Both gestures are ALWAYS available - no choice can build a firmware without the physical factory reset."

    config MICHI_BUTTON_DEBOUNCE_MS
        int "Debounce window (ms)"
        default 30
        range 10 200
        help
          Stable-window debounce: an edge (press/release) is confirmed only
          after the GPIO level stays equal for a full wall-clock window of
          this many milliseconds (measured by the pure debouncer in
          michi_button_debounce.c, fed by the polling task). The poll period
          does NOT gate the window, so POLL >= DEBOUNCE no longer disables
          the debounce. Honest guarantee: a glitch shorter than this window
          is rejected by the single-authority state machine; contacts that
          bounce for longer than the window need a larger value.
          30 ms rejects most contact chatter while preserving clean taps

    config MICHI_BUTTON_MIN_PRESS_MS
        int "Minimum valid press duration (ms)"
        default 50
        range 5 500
        help
          Press durations shorter than this are treated as noise and
          discarded. Default 50 ms is below any intentional human gesture
          but above typical contact chatter. Must be less than
          MICHI_BUTTON_RECOVERY_PRESS_MS.

    config MICHI_BUTTON_PAIRING_HOLD_MS
        int "Pairing hold threshold (ms)"
        default 5000
        range 2000 30000
        help
          Duration the button must be held (without release) before the
          pairing window opens (hold-on-threshold contract, P0-01). The
          action fires at the MOMENT the elapsed time crosses this value,
          not when the button is released. In RECOVERABLE_ERROR state the
          same threshold triggers recovery instead of pairing.
          5000 ms is long enough to avoid accidental triggers.
          Must be < MICHI_BUTTON_FACTORY_WARN_MS.

    config MICHI_BUTTON_FACTORY_WARN_MS
        int "Factory-reset warning threshold (ms)"
        default 10000
        range MICHI_BUTTON_PAIRING_HOLD_MS 60000
        help
          If the button is still held after this duration AND the pairing
          action was NOT fired (gesture not consumed), a visual/audio
          warning is shown indicating that releasing now cancels the press
          but continued holding will trigger a factory reset.
          Must be > PAIRING_HOLD_MS and < FACTORY_RESET_PRESS_MS.

    config MICHI_BUTTON_FACTORY_RESET_PRESS_MS
        int "Factory reset hold threshold (ms)"
        default 15000
        range MICHI_BUTTON_FACTORY_WARN_MS 60000
        help
          Duration the button must be held to trigger factory reset.  Only
          fires if the gesture is NOT already consumed (pairing/recovery did
          not fire earlier in the same press), preventing accidental
          escalation from pairing to reset.  The press must also have
          started at least MICHI_BUTTON_FACTORY_ARM_MS after boot.
          15 s is deliberately above the 10 s warning to give time to
          release.

    config MICHI_BUTTON_FACTORY_ARM_MS
        int "Factory reset arm window (ms)"
        default 10000
        range 0 300000
        help
          A factory reset runs only if the press STARTED at least this many
          milliseconds after boot (measured with esp_timer_get_time()
          against the button init reference). A button held through
          power-on, or a stuck pin, would otherwise confirm a "press" with
          ~0 ms elapsed as soon as the FSM leaves the protected states and
          erase NVS. 0 disables the arm window. Recovery is NOT gated by
          the arm window (a recoverable error right after boot must stay
          recoverable).

    config MICHI_BUTTON_POLL_MS
        int "Debounce task poll period (ms)"
        default 5
        range 1 50
        help
          Sampling period of the debounce task. Each sample is fed to the
          pure single-authority debouncer (michi_button_debounce.c), which
          confirms an edge only after the level is stable for a full
          MICHI_BUTTON_DEBOUNCE_MS wall-clock window; the poll period does
          NOT gate that window (a sub-window bounce is rejected by the
          stable-state machine itself, not by sample counting). The poll
          cadence sets the task's wake rate and the granularity of the
          idle current; 5 ms gives 200 samples/s of a single GPIO read.

    config MICHI_BUTTON_TASK_STACK_BYTES
        int "Debounce task stack (bytes)"
        default 3072
        range 2048 16384
        help
          Stack of the debounce task (ESP-IDF xTaskCreate takes bytes).
          The task polls one GPIO and posts events, so the default is
          generous.

endmenu
